<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>International news from the Americas - France 24</title><description>FRANCE 24’s coverage of the political, social and economic issues in the United States, Canada, Mexico, Argentina, Brazil and across the Americas.</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/</link><lastBuildDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 17:29:40 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category></category><title>Brazil election: Lula vows to stand up to Trump</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/brazil-election-lula-vows-to-stand-up-to-trump</link><description>
Brazilian President Lula says he will confront President Donald Trump at the UN in New York, accusing him of interfering in Brazil's election as tensions between Washington and Brasília deepen. The dispute comes after US tariffs on Brazilian goods and Trump's support for Lula's rival, Flavio Bolsonaro, the son of former president Jair Bolsonaro.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/345cc18c-8e95-11f1-b4f7-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C3TD7FG.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/345cc18c-8e95-11f1-b4f7-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C3TD7FG.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">24a7f6b0-b2a5-11f1-afaa-2fac250903fa</guid><pubDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 14:47:39 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>US interest rate hike sparks Trump backlash</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/us-interest-rate-hike-sparks-trump-backlash</link><description>
The US Federal Reserve has raised interest rates for the first time since 2023, citing stubborn inflation despite pressure from President Donald Trump to cut borrowing costs. The decision prompted an immediate rebuke from Trump, while Fed Chair Kevin Warsh defended the central bank's independence and warned that inflation remains the priority.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/46cfe290-b29e-11f1-bac2-4daf57bffe27/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260917-140754-140925-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/46cfe290-b29e-11f1-bac2-4daf57bffe27/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260917-140754-140925-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4cccbb28-b29e-11f1-bbf0-0bf69855a15f</guid><pubDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 14:21:23 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Mark Carney's EU speech highlights Canada's shifting alliances</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260917-mark-carney-s-eu-speech-highlights-canada-s-shifting-alliances-1</link><description>
Canadian Prime Minister Mark Carney addressed the European Parliament as Ottawa and Brussels deepen ties against a backdrop of strained relations with the United States. FRANCE 24's Doug Herbert explains how the speech illustrates a broader shift in alliances, with a message that, until recently, would more likely have been delivered in Washington than Brussels.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9fb7a19a-b28a-11f1-b70e-a1d0582895b1/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260917-120914-121514-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9fb7a19a-b28a-11f1-b70e-a1d0582895b1/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260917-120914-121514-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a47c62f6-b28a-11f1-9a68-51f62954151d</guid><pubDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 11:37:31 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>US Congress passes Russia sanctions bill</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/us-congress-passes-russia-sanctions-bill</link><description>
The US Congress has approved a sweeping Russia sanctions bill, sending it to President Donald Trump for final approval as Washington seeks to increase pressure on Moscow over the war in Ukraine.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bfa9a852-b27d-11f1-946d-6db10b20ba37/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260917-101258-101433-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bfa9a852-b27d-11f1-946d-6db10b20ba37/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260917-101258-101433-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c4d93194-b27d-11f1-8f72-679ef28c9d07</guid><pubDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 10:26:32 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>US again denies Palestinian leader visa for UN General Assembly</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260917-us-palestinian-leader-visa-un-general-assembly-new-york</link><description>
The United States has denied Palestinian President Mahmoud Abbas a visa to attend next week's UN General Assembly in New York, a source familiar with the matter said on Wednesday. The State Department separately said it would deny visas to Palestinian officials, citing failures to reform and actions it said undermined peace prospects.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4ed18198-b23e-11f1-afcc-4daf57bffe27/w:1024/p:16x9/Abbas-3.jpeg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4ed18198-b23e-11f1-afcc-4daf57bffe27/w:1024/p:16x9/Abbas-3.jpeg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">613af3e6-b243-11f1-aa47-b96ea4579081</guid><pubDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 03:03:25 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4ed18198-b23e-11f1-afcc-4daf57bffe27/w:1024/p:16x9/Abbas-3.jpeg">© AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>US House holds billionaire Epstein associate Leon Black in contempt of Congress</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260916-leon-black-epstein-contempt-congress</link><description>
The US House of Representatives on Wednesday held billionaire investor Leon Black in contempt of Congress for defying two subpoenas in its investigation into sex offender Jeffrey Epstein. The measure passed by unanimous consent and will be referred to the Justice Department, which will decide whether to pursue criminal charges.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e46f3684-b21e-11f1-9edf-4daf57bffe27/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26246480870989.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e46f3684-b21e-11f1-9edf-4daf57bffe27/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26246480870989.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">801165ea-b21e-11f1-95a9-855106d3699b</guid><pubDate>Wed, 16 Sep 2026 22:37:03 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e46f3684-b21e-11f1-9edf-4daf57bffe27/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26246480870989.jpg">© J. Scott Applewhite, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>US announces charges against five alleged agents for Russia over assassination plots</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260916-us-announces-charges-against-five-alleged-agents-for-russia-over-assassination-plots</link><description>
The US Department of Justice announced on Tuesday charges against five alleged Russian intelligence agents accused of recruiting a global network to conspire attacks and carry out assassinations by order of the Kremlin. The suspects remain at large.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9fe0d04a-b1ab-11f1-a1ba-f72ea3a769d9/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26254519545366.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9fe0d04a-b1ab-11f1-a1ba-f72ea3a769d9/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26254519545366.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3ce8a948-b1ad-11f1-9d43-177d59d5ca13</guid><pubDate>Wed, 16 Sep 2026 09:13:24 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9fe0d04a-b1ab-11f1-a1ba-f72ea3a769d9/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26254519545366.jpg">© Julia Demaree Nikhinson, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Ed Sheeran's tour in trouble after Pro-Palestine acts drop out</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260916-ed-sheeran-s-tour-in-trouble-after-pro-palestine-acts-drop-out</link><description>
More artists scheduled to participate in Ed Sheeran’s tour of North and South America have quit in solidarity with the rapper Macklemore, who was dropped for making pro-Palestinian comments onstage. Among them are Irish acts Rowe and Lukas Graham, as well as Billie Eilish’s brother, Finneas.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6a7781b4-b198-11f1-97c0-cfc9bd8e913f/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26257691242503.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6a7781b4-b198-11f1-97c0-cfc9bd8e913f/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26257691242503.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b6138d66-b198-11f1-8ca8-9164e56b78fd</guid><pubDate>Wed, 16 Sep 2026 06:54:21 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6a7781b4-b198-11f1-97c0-cfc9bd8e913f/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26257691242503.jpg">© Andy Kropa, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>NBC news helicopter crashes in LA while covering bus collision, killing three</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260916-media-helicopter-crashes-in-la-while-covering-bus-collision-killing-three</link><description>
A news helicopter covering a deadly bus crash in the Los Angeles neighbourhood of Chatsworth came down on Tuesday, killing three people, including a pedestrian.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2d052580-b188-11f1-8b35-3ff9dda05487/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26259123487034.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2d052580-b188-11f1-8b35-3ff9dda05487/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26259123487034.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e7df3910-b186-11f1-b3f3-7165d3a52c31</guid><pubDate>Wed, 16 Sep 2026 04:47:53 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2d052580-b188-11f1-8b35-3ff9dda05487/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26259123487034.jpg">© AP via KABC-TV</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>New French ambassador to US cleared to take up post after diplomatic spat</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260916-new-french-ambassador-to-us-cleared-to-take-up-post-after-diplomatic-spat</link><description>
France's incoming ambassador to the US has been cleared to take up his post after Paris apologised for criticism of Washington over a UN vote. Aurélien Lechevallier, chosen by President Emmanuel Macron to replace Laurent Bili, is expected to arrive in Washington in the coming weeks following the diplomatic dispute.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5c9fb67c-b177-11f1-9c05-53b7617a3a51/w:1024/p:16x9/AP24012249631357.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5c9fb67c-b177-11f1-9c05-53b7617a3a51/w:1024/p:16x9/AP24012249631357.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">22dd122c-b17c-11f1-9c1d-173f3a2cee65</guid><pubDate>Wed, 16 Sep 2026 03:10:13 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5c9fb67c-b177-11f1-9c05-53b7617a3a51/w:1024/p:16x9/AP24012249631357.jpg">© Ludovic Marin, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Trump says renovation of Kennedy Center depends on whether his name is on it</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260915-trump-threatens-to-not-reopen-kennedy-center-after-board-blocks-renaming</link><description>
The Kennedy Center board voted Tuesday to close most of the Washington performing arts complex for safety repairs, hours after a judge again blocked efforts to add President Donald Trump’s name to the building. Trump said the $257 million renovation plan depended on recognising his role in the project.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7e9f8c48-b14f-11f1-9746-53b7617a3a51/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26258780756063.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7e9f8c48-b14f-11f1-9746-53b7617a3a51/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26258780756063.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">80cf5e86-b153-11f1-989f-d976d60b5816</guid><pubDate>Tue, 15 Sep 2026 22:19:21 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7e9f8c48-b14f-11f1-9746-53b7617a3a51/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26258780756063.jpg">© Jacquelyn Martin, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>'Canada can offer a more reliable route for energy exports to the EU', expert says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/canada-can-offer-a-more-reliable-route-for-energy-exports-to-the-eu-expert-says</link><description>
Speaking with FRANCE 24's Mark Owen, Dr. Walaa-Eldeen Bakry, Principal Lecturer in Project Management and Finance and Director of Executive Education at Westminster Business School, says that "Carney is deliberately aiming to diversify the Canadian trade policy", explaining that it "can actually offer a more reliable route in terms of energy exports from Canada into the EU and we have seen last year a significant increase in oil exports to some European countries".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3209cae6-b13c-11f1-b26a-cfc9bd8e913f/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260915-210701-211432-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3209cae6-b13c-11f1-b26a-cfc9bd8e913f/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260915-210701-211432-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3876868a-b13c-11f1-bfa8-4597b21ce242</guid><pubDate>Tue, 15 Sep 2026 19:42:08 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Spotlight</category><title>'Revolutionary change in US foreign policy: MAGA does not see itself as leader of democratic world'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260915-revolutionary-change-in-american-foreign-policy-canada-pivoting-towards-eu-india-and-china</link><description>
For Spotlight, FRANCE 24 François Picard is pleased to welcome Anne Applebaum, staff writer at The Atlantic and author of Autocracy, Inc. According to Applebaum, the upheaval in American diplomacy and foreign policy transcends any one administration. She describes a full-fledged transformation in the way the United States exerts power, pivoting away from leadership of a democratic alliance and toward a transactional, mafia-style politics that fuses ideology, private economic interests, personal relationships and geopolitical leverage.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/28267f10-b137-11f1-acba-53b7617a3a51/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260915-181125-182631-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/28267f10-b137-11f1-acba-53b7617a3a51/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260915-181125-182631-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">468bd06a-b13a-11f1-918b-aba208a208d7</guid><pubDate>Tue, 15 Sep 2026 19:18:43 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>François PICARD</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Canada's Carney seeks closer Europe ties to counter hostile US</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/canada-s-carney-seeks-closer-europe-ties-to-counter-hostile-us</link><description>
Canadian Prime Minister Mark Carney is heading to Europe in the middle of a trade war with U.S. President Donald Trump, seeking a deeper relationship with the European Union that could give Canadians greater freedom to work and study there. FRANCE 24's Christopher Guly reports from Ottawa.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e49123dc-a087-11f1-8dc3-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-24T163056Z-1186857443-RC2R3NAM318W-RTRMADP-3-CANADA-DEFENSE-ICEBREAKERS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e49123dc-a087-11f1-8dc3-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-24T163056Z-1186857443-RC2R3NAM318W-RTRMADP-3-CANADA-DEFENSE-ICEBREAKERS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d4a1d3ee-b136-11f1-81fa-f76b9ab306f7</guid><pubDate>Tue, 15 Sep 2026 18:57:48 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>US acknowledges for the first time that it has deployed weapons in space</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/us-acknowledges-for-the-first-time-that-it-has-deployed-weapons-in-space</link><description>
The United States has confirmed for the first time that it has deployed weapons in space, a remarkable revelation after previous warnings about countries such as Russia possibly weaponizing a global frontier long agreed in treaties to be used for only peaceful purposes. FRANCE 24's Emerald Maxwell reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/20a13fd6-b133-11f1-ac78-3ff9dda05487/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260915-201100-201302-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/20a13fd6-b133-11f1-ac78-3ff9dda05487/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260915-201100-201302-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">26890780-b133-11f1-9948-c3dcfe0b9fe0</guid><pubDate>Tue, 15 Sep 2026 18:34:46 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Focus</category><title>Rapid data center expansion incites backlash in Republican stronghold</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20260915-rapid-data-center-expansion-incites-backlash-in-republican-stronghold</link><description>
With just a couple months to go until the US midterm election, a new political fault line is emerging in Republican strongholds across Texas driven by the rapid expansion of artificial intelligence. According to an analysis by the Texas Tribune, nearly 60 percent of planned new data centers are set to be built in congressional districts that voted for Donald Trump in 2024. But the AI boom is now sparking a backlash from some of the voters who helped put him back in office. Pierrick Leurent and Valérie Defert have this report.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fd51f178-b043-11f1-87fa-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/PASDEREF-FOCUS-EN-Data-Centers-Texas-CORNET-0309.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fd51f178-b043-11f1-87fa-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/PASDEREF-FOCUS-EN-Data-Centers-Texas-CORNET-0309.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c7b9770a-b04a-11f1-8479-7d9d3b14ed80</guid><pubDate>Tue, 15 Sep 2026 15:05:44 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Pierrick LEURENT</dc:creator></item><item><category>Spotlight</category><title>Corruption ‘endemic’ in Trump administration: 'Checks and balances only in effect at lower courts'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260915-corruption-endemic-in-trump-administration-checks-and-balances-only-in-effect-at-lower-courts</link><description>
François Picard is pleased to welcome Andrew Weissmann, Author, Professor at NYU School of Law, and former General Counsel of the FBI. He argues that as political deception and deliberate falsehoods become normalized, and politically useful, it erodes any trust we have in our government and our institutions. Drawing on his book, "Liar’s Kingdom", Weissmann questions why political leaders are above the law in the United States, while ordinary citizens risk serious legal consequences for making intentionally false statements.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/134880ea-b0b3-11f1-871a-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260914-180947-182810-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/134880ea-b0b3-11f1-871a-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260914-180947-182810-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">74a4dd9e-b0da-11f1-9bd1-b95f3054049f</guid><pubDate>Tue, 15 Sep 2026 07:52:51 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>François PICARD</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Iran war exposes US munitions shortfall, industrial bottlenecks, Pentagon report says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260915-iran-war-exposes-us-munitions-shortfall-industrial-bottlenecks-pentagon-report-says</link><description>
The US military faces shortages of key munitions due to the Iran war and industrial "bottlenecks" to rebuild stockpiles, a Pentagon watchdog warned in a report published on Monday, contradicting US President Donald Trump's assurances that ammunition supplies are "virtually unlimited".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/76716e8e-b0c7-11f1-9d6d-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C8744CR.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/76716e8e-b0c7-11f1-9d6d-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C8744CR.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">26def974-b0ca-11f1-8bd4-757e8e613dcc</guid><pubDate>Tue, 15 Sep 2026 06:07:23 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/76716e8e-b0c7-11f1-9d6d-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C8744CR.jpg">© US Navy via AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Venezuela to join G20 energy talks in Texas at US invitation</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260915-venezuela-to-join-g20-energy-meetings-in-texas-at-us-invitation</link><description>
A Venezuelan delegation will join G20 energy talks in Houston this week as soaring oil prices and disruption from the Middle East war put global energy supplies under pressure. The meeting comes as the Trump administration deepens energy ties with Caracas and seeks to boost Venezuelan oil output.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/47d96d1c-b098-11f1-9021-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/ea7607de8aa30c2ff2134ead7b6e53246246fe8f.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/47d96d1c-b098-11f1-9021-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/ea7607de8aa30c2ff2134ead7b6e53246246fe8f.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6a5aff92-b0af-11f1-8158-3570f775cb63</guid><pubDate>Tue, 15 Sep 2026 02:44:46 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/47d96d1c-b098-11f1-9021-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/ea7607de8aa30c2ff2134ead7b6e53246246fe8f.jpg">© Ronaldo Schemidt, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>US Supreme Court rejects Trump bid to restrict mail ballots as voting begins</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260915-us-supreme-court-rejects-trump-bid-to-restrict-mail-ballots-as-voting-begins</link><description>
The US Supreme Court on Monday rejected President Donald Trump’s bid to impose new restrictions on mail ballots ahead of November’s midterm elections. The ruling leaves states free to continue using existing voting procedures, after election officials warned the last-minute changes could disrupt ballot distribution.
